## 2. Inline Commenting Best Practices

- Use inline comments for non-obvious business logic, "why" decisions, or to clarify intent—never to restate code.
- Place comments above the line(s) they clarify, not beside (unless for short explanations).
- Use section comments to break up and identify distinct computation blocks in longer functions.
- Update or remove comments as code evolves to avoid misleading documentation.

```python
# Apply bonus interest only for legacy accounts (opened before 2010)
if user.join_year < 2010:
    apply_bonus_interest(user)
```

---

### Special Inline Comments

- Use TODO, FIXME, NOTE, HACK, and similar conventions with your name/initials and date for traceability.

```python
# TODO(jane, 2024-06): Migrate to async logic when endpoint supports it.
```

